    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'm just wondering though... if at the end of the day these 'character' arguments are really just excuses to keep housing prices high and stop new people from moving in, isn't it kind of counterproductive to treat them as equal concerns? it feels like we're just giving a platform to NIMBYism which actually harms the city in the long run. wouldn't a more honest approach be to point out that these objections are statistically and economically outdated?",
